Close https://github.com/prisma/team-orm/issues/410

This patch overcomes a long-time limitation in quaint, which is that it's main model was an enum, which required chaning all variants to include data common to all types.

We need this because in driver adapters, it's not possible to achieve full correctness unless we implement conversions similarly to those of quiant, for instance, in postgres, we convert data types based on a combination of the prisma data type for a scalar, and its native type.

```rust
         (Value::DateTime(value), &PostgresType::TIME) => value.map(|value| value.time().to_sql(ty, out)),
            (Value::DateTime(value), &PostgresType::TIMETZ) => value.map(|value| {
                let result = value.time().to_sql(ty, out)?;
                // We assume UTC. see https://www.postgresql.org/docs/9.5/datatype-datetime.html
                out.extend_from_slice(&[0; 4]);
                Ok(result)
            }),
```

This is possible in rust quaint because the postgres rust driver has an in memory cache of the database column types. But in driver adapters we don't have that information available and we need to provide it in the quaint representation of a query, and with the current design of a `quaint::Value` that is not possible.

In summary, this PR allows for correct data type conversions for driver adapters which otherwise won't be possible.

## what Change does this PR introduce?
This PR Fixes Darkmode button when we click on a Darkmode button nothing happen;

Fixes #22;

### What does it do?

Updates the Combobox rendered value if the corresponding prop changes "externally" (without clicking an option)

### Why is it needed?

Because if the prop changes, the "internal" value is actually updated but the rendered text not

### How to test it?

I tested this manually, let me know if I should update UT

```
// docs/stories/Combobox.stories.tsx

export const Depending = {
  render: () => {
    const [value, setValue] = useState('');

    const options = ['apple', 'avocado', 'banana', 'kiwi', 'mango', 'orange', 'strawberry'];

    const handleChange = (index) => {
      setValue(options[index]);
    };

    return (
      <Flex direction="column" alignItems="stretch" gap={11}>
        {options.map((option, index) => (
          <Button key={index} onClick={() => handleChange(index)}>
            {index}
          </Button>
        ))}
        <span style={{ color: 'white' }}>{value}</span>
        <Combobox
          placeholder="My favourite fruit is..."
          label="Fruits"
          value={value}
          onChange={setValue}
          onClear={() => setValue('')}
        >
          {options.map((option) => (
            <ComboboxOption key={option} value={option}>
              {option}
            </ComboboxOption>
          ))}
        </Combobox>
      </Flex>
    );
  },

  name: 'depending',
} satisfies Story;

```

